          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em modular form
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+function"} holomorphic function
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+half-plane"} upper half-plane
            that satisfies certain transformation property under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+group"} modular group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of a certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+half+plane"} upper half plane
            that makes it the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
            (over the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+curve"} modular curve
          %p
            Modular forms are also often called
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                classical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphic+forms"} automorphic forms
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => ""} below
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Langlands+program"} Langlands program
          %p
            Modular forms appear as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficient"} coefficient
            ring of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            on manifolds with rational
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            this refines to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+modular+forms"} topological modular forms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
